{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f583052f2aa9407a","name":"GE3-Series Protocol Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-f583052f2aa9407a","title":"GE3-Series Protocol Droid","revision":19145,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:24:14Z","sha256":"605f3f8b569de1291f8a2a7e4dba9ef8830dbf54b0d3507c318e9abe39de68d3","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19145","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=GE3-Series%20Protocol%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f583052f2aa9407a","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["One of the best-selling Droids in the galaxy, the Czerka Corporation's GE3-Series Multipurpose Protocol Droid is found everywhere from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"}," to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"}," and beyond. One of the most common humanoid ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Models"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Models"},", the GE3-Series Protocol Droid primarily serves as an agent of Human-Cyborg relations, but can be programmed to fill a variety of roles. Some GE3-Series Droids are used as liaisons between farmers and their machinery; others serve as personal secretaries and errand-runners for busy citizens on urban worlds. These Droids serve a variety of tasks, from menial chores to assisting in galactic negotiations, and as such they are highly valued by citizens, both high and low on the power ladder.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The GE-3-Series programming is geared specifically toward social interaction. They are extremely knowledgeable about the customs, cultures, and histories of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," throughout the galaxy, and serve as the standard for Protocol Droids for decades. GE3-Series Protocol Droids are used in domestic and political environments, and ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Czerka Corporation"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Czerka_Corporation","referenceId":"reference:cf6b7a4dee7c0713"}," has a longstanding policy of selling these Droids to planetary governments in bulk at a discounted rate, ensuring that their Droids are found on nearly every planet in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"},". Though technically all GE3-Series Protocol Droids share the same suffix to their names (GE3), most shorten their designation to contain only their unique identifier; thus, a protocol Droid whose full designation would be S-0D3-GE3 would drop the GE3, and would go by only S-0D3.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["GE3-Series Protocol Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["GE3-Series Protocol Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["3rd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3rd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +0; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +2\n"]